Package: fitcheck
Type: Package
Title: Check the Data, Then the Solution, Then the Fit, for Second-Order Factor Models
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Salman", "Rashid", email = "salman41pasca.2023@student.uny.ac.id", role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Heri", "Retnawati", role = "aut"),
    person("Samsul", "Hadi", role = "aut"))
Description: A workflow for judging second-order confirmatory factor models fitted to
    operational test data. It screens records with no real responses before
    any model is fitted, shows whether screening changes the measurement
    evidence within each test form and across forms (measurement invariance
    with and without the flagged records), checks that a solution is
    admissible under two identifications before fit is read, reports the
    unbiased standardized root mean square residual with its interval
    (Maydeu-Olivares, 2017, <doi:10.1007/s11336-016-9552-7>), shows how
    estimation and fit would behave in smaller samples of the user's own
    data, and tests whether section scores add value over the total score
    (Haberman, 2008, <doi:10.3102/1076998607302636>). Built on 'lavaan'.
